<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The character editor: everything about one pawn, and a list of the colony to pick from.

    order 43 puts it after the corpses tab (42), which is where it belongs: the editor is what the
    corpses tab hands a body to when the answer is to bring them back.

    THIS TAB DOES NOT ALWAYS EXIST. A MainButtonDef cannot be conditionally undefined, so the button
    is hidden by UIButtonBarConfig.Suppressed whenever the character editor setting is off, which is
    its default. With the setting off there is no button on the bar and no way to open the window.

    No defaultHotKey, deliberately. A key that opens a tool for rewriting pawns is a key somebody
    presses by accident, and there is no vanilla binding this replaces.

    validWithoutMap is false: the roster is read off a map's pawns, so there is nothing to show from
    the main menu or the world view.
  -->
  <MainButtonDef>
    <defName>Gideon_CharacterEditor</defName>
    <label>editor</label>
    <description>Change anything about one of your pawns: name, age, sex, looks, backstory, traits, skills, genes, health, needs, thoughts, gear and relationships. On a dead pawn it can also bring them back. Characters can be saved to a file and applied to somebody else, or imported into another colony entirely.\n\nThis tab only appears while the character editor is switched on under Additional Features.</description>
    <tabWindowClass>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Editor.MainTabWindow_CharacterEditor</tabWindowClass>
    <validWithoutMap>false</validWithoutMap>
    <closesWorldView>true</closesWorldView>

    <!--
      No file extension and no Textures prefix: RimWorld's ContentFinder takes a path relative to
      Textures and appends the extension itself. A bust with a pencil, drawn for this tab in the same
      flat grayscale as the rest of the family so it tints with the palette.
    -->
    <iconPath>UI/MainButtonIcons/CharacterEditor</iconPath>

    <order>43</order>
  </MainButtonDef>

</Defs>
